 @Sureflame  The PS5 uses a custom AMD APU and its limiting factor is its CPU in that APU. x3D could not work for a Console because x3D isn't a custom SoC. 

Consoles require a lot more engineering to work properly than a PC. So thermal capacity and dissipation of heat are also factors in building consoles.

The games are purposely made shackled like that there won't ever be a console that "unlocks" your games like just upgrading PC hardware.. cause if that was the case ALL PS4 games would run better and they don't.

 @JohnWiku  ah I see

Yeah that's clearly an unfortunate loss

It's just not "fuses" xd

 @emperorcaligula5786  Sure consoles are subsidized, but they never had $1200 PC equivalent value. Ignoring recent GPU-price insanity. Like the PS4 had a CPU that was worse than most gaming laptops, and a pathetic amount of memory. GPU was better, but also more like an older mid-end model. 

To me I just take PC over Consoles tho, even if its a bit more expensive. Gets me stuff like the ability to play an infinite number of old games, sometimes with modern upgrades patches/mods. Or tuning peformance, so I can limit input-lag, disable stuff like motion blur and enjoy high FPS-gaming if I want to. 
On consoles even gaming at 60fps is a luxury that not every game offers.

 @pem3480  That is basically it, too. Even with all of these reviewers complaining online, people will look at how shit the prices on everything else is and buy it anyway. It is like we are living in another great depression, but people are just comfortable enough not to even complain like generations past. 

The people complaining in comment sections and the reviewers represent maybe a very tiny minority of the PC gaming scene alone. Most people will sadly doomspend just so that they feel something is going well in their lives. It's sad, but most people are sheep. The only way this actually gets better is through a revolution, but so long as the bread and circuses, PC gaming being the latter, remain just barely affordable for the pleb, nothing will ever happen. 

Humans will sadly endure comical levels of bullshit so long as they are somewhat comfortable.
